# Start Light firmware

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing behavior. Deployable code lives only in `firmware/`. Docs live in `docs/` and must never be copied to the Pico (tiny flash).

Git is trunk-based: never push to `main`. Use `feature/<name>` (or `fix/` / `docs/` / `chore/`), open a PR, squash or rebase merge. See `docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`.

This is MicroPython on a Raspberry Pi **Pico 2 W** (preferred) or Pico W. Flash `RPI_PICO2_W` or `RPI_PICO_W` UF2 to match the hardware — UF2s are not interchangeable; `.py` app code is. There is no pip, no asyncio, and no CPython-only stdlib. On-device imports are flat (`from lights import …`) because `.py` files are copied to the Pico root.

## Invariants

- Lamps are active-low. `Pin.value(0)` is ON, `Pin.value(1)` is OFF. Boot and cleanup must leave every lamp OFF.

```python
# ON
pin.value(0)
# OFF
pin.value(1)
```

- WiFi STA and BLE share one radio. Call `wlan.active(False)` before `bluetooth.BLE()`. Do not serve HTTP while BLE is advertising.
- `firmware/main.py` owns boot: self-test, WiFi retries, BLE credential mode, optional IP-over-BLE, then the start loop. Do not add a second entry point.
- One start implementation: `LightController.run_start_sequence`. Web `/start` and BLE `START` / `GO` / `RUN` must both call it.
- Defaults live in `firmware/config.py`. The Pico overrides them in `startlight_config.json` through `firmware/settings.py`. Do not add another settings store.
- `PREFERRED_NETWORK` and `GREEN_AFTER_LAST_YELLOW` are unused. Wire them up or leave them; do not assume they already affect the sequence.
- Never commit `wifi_creds.json`, `wifi_networks.json`, or the other paths in `.gitignore`.

## When extending

- Keep the web UI as inline HTML in `firmware/webserver.py`. A settings POST must call `settings.save`.
- Reflect status on the lamps (`lights.blink_status`), the onboard LED (`onboard_led`), and the OLED (`display.py`). OLED uses SoftI2C on GP6/GP7 (probe 0x3C then 0x3D); hard I2C ETIMEDOUT/EIO is a known RP2 issue. A missing OLED must not abort boot.
- `run_server` accepts one connection, then returns. The start sequence blocks that loop until the lamps finish.
- Put new documentation under `docs/`. Put new device code under `firmware/` as `.py` only.
